# 🤖 3-Wheel Robot — Self-Balancing WiFi-Controlled Robot

A fully custom-built, two-wheel self-balancing robot designed and engineered from scratch. This includes a custom-designed chassis, a purpose-built PCB, and firmware for remote control over WiFi.

---

## 📖 Project Overview

This project describes a **2-wheel balance robot system**. While many designs exist online, every component here was built from the ground up:

- 🏗️ **Chassis** designed in [OnShape](https://www.onshape.com/)
- 🔌 **Custom PCB** integrating motor drivers, IMU, encoders, and WiFi
- 📱 **Remote control** via WiFi using a smartphone
- ⚖️ **Active balancing** using sensor fusion and a control loop
- 🎯 **Additional challenge layer** planned to spice up the balancing system

> The robot started as a 3-wheel platform. The ball wheel was later removed to transition to a 2-wheel self-balancing configuration — making balance control a core challenge.

---

## ✨ Features

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| **Microcontroller** | STM32F401RBT6 — 64-pin LQFP package |
| **Chassis** | Custom design via OnShape CAD |
| **PCB** | Fully custom board designed in-house |
| **Motor Driver** | Integrated on PCB |
| **IMU** | On-board inertial measurement unit for balancing |
| **Encoders** | Motor encoders for closed-loop control |
| **Connectivity** | WiFi shield for smartphone remote control |
| **Interfaces Used** | Timers, PWM, Encoders, I2C, UART |

---

## 🛠️ Hardware

### Microcontroller
The **STM32F401RBT6** was chosen for its rich peripheral support. Pins were carefully selected to interface all required hardware using:
- **Timers & PWM** — Motor speed control
- **Encoders** — Motor position/velocity feedback
- **I2C** — IMU communication
- **UART** — Debugging and serial communication

### PCB
The custom PCB integrates all components onto a single board:
- Motor driver circuitry
- IMU sensor
- Encoder interfaces
- WiFi shield connectivity

### Chassis
Designed from scratch in **OnShape**, optimized for the balancing dynamics of a 2-wheel configuration.

